# RealScout & Vercel

## RealScout

- Two domains required in CSP: script from `em.realscout.com`, API from `www.realscout.com` — both in `script-src` and `connect-src` in `next.config.ts`
- Load script once globally in root layout via `<Script>`
- Use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` for widget components; don't load script multiple times

## Vercel + DNS

- Prefer `vercel build` (or `vercel --prod`) for production builds over local `pnpm build`
- When using Vercel, don't proxy through Cloudflare (orange cloud) — use DNS only (gray cloud) to avoid SSL conflicts

## Cloudflare Error 1027 (Workers plan / quota)

This is **not** fixable in Next.js code. It means the **Cloudflare account** hit Workers (or related) limits for that hostname.

**If the live app is on Vercel:** In Cloudflare DNS for the domain, set records that point to Vercel to **DNS only** (gray cloud). Remove unnecessary **Workers Routes** or **Page Rules** that invoke a Worker on that host. That stops edge Worker usage for that zone so traffic goes to Vercel without exhausting Workers quota.

**If the app uses Cloudflare Workers or Pages Functions:** In [Cloudflare Dashboard → Workers & Pages](https://dash.cloudflare.com/), open **Metrics**, identify spikes (traffic, bots, cron). Either **upgrade the Workers plan** / add paid capacity, or reduce invocations (cache, shorter Worker logic, block abusive IPs in WAF).

**Visitors:** Wait or contact the site owner; only the Cloudflare account holder can resolve quota.

## IDX/MLS

- Always display MLS disclaimer and listing attribution
- Don't modify `/components/idx/*` without explicit approval
